===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|trebuchets|lang=fro}}, {{term|trebuket}} et al. (modern {{term|trébuchet}}), from {{term|trabucher||to overthrow}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|trabuchare}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛbəʃɛt/|/ˈtɹɛb.jə.ʃeɪ/|/ˈtɹɛb.ju.ʃeɪ/}}; {{SAMPA|/"trEb.j@.SeI/|/"trEb.jU.SeI/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|trěb’yo͞o-shet}}, {{IPA|/ˈtɹɛb.juˌʃɛt/|/ˈtɹɛb.jəˌʃeɪ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A medieval [[siege engine]] consisting of a large pivoting arm heavily weighted on one end.  Considered to be the technological successor to the [[catapult]].

